---
layout: layouts/product.njk
permalink: /enterprise/migration/
title: "Vendor consolidation and migration for enterprise"
description: "Consolidate voice, numbers, PBX, SIP, and applications under one operational relationship. Line-item pricing plus cost modeling against actual usage."
---
{%- from "partials/v2/macros.njk" import arrow %}
{%- set years %}{% yearsSince 1999 %}{% endset %}

<section class="hero hero--page" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
	<div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="container hero__inner">
		<div class="hero__copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Enterprise migration</p>
			<h1 id="hero-heading">Consolidate voice, numbers, PBX, SIP, and applications.</h1>
			<p class="lede">Enterprise communications fragment over time: one provider for SIP trunks, another for numbers, others for messaging, PBX, apps, porting, and support. VoiceTel brings wholesale voice, SIP trunking, numbers and porting, Hosted PBX, phone applications, messaging, lookups, and VoiceML under one operational relationship.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact/">Talk to VoiceTel {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--secondary btn--lg" href="/pricing/">Model your monthly spend</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero__visual">
			{%- set diagram = {
				title: "From one provider per service, through a cost model, to one operational relationship",
				nodes: [
					{ label: "Today", value: "One provider per service", meta: "SIP · numbers · messaging · PBX", icon: "layers" },
					{ label: "Migration plan", value: "Modeled from invoices and CDRs", meta: "porting · cutover · rollback", icon: "arrow-right-circle", accent: true },
					{ label: "VoiceTel", value: "One operational relationship", meta: "voice · numbers · PBX · apps", icon: "buildings" }
				],
				links: [
					{ label: "model", accent: true },
					{ label: "migrate" }
				],
				meta: [
					{ k: "Rates", v: "published list rates, line-item" },
					{ k: "Tiers", v: "volume or contract, shown in the portal" },
					{ k: "Operating since", v: "1999" }
				]
			} %}
			{% include "partials/v2/diagram.njk" %}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="support" aria-labelledby="support-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">What VoiceTel can support</p>
			<h2 id="support-heading">Branch modernization, vendor consolidation, employee mobility, carrier migration, and cost modeling.</h2>
		</div>
		{%- set features = [
			{ icon: "buildings", title: "Branch modernization", body: "Move legacy voice services into a more flexible SIP, PBX, or app-based model." },
			{ icon: "layers", title: "Vendor consolidation", body: "Voice, numbers, applications, and routing under one operational relationship." },
			{ icon: "phone-vibrate", title: "Employee mobility", body: "Users across desktop, browser, and mobile environments." },
			{ icon: "arrow-right-circle", title: "Carrier migration", body: "Porting, cutover windows, rollback paths, and e911 updates." },
			{ icon: "tag", title: "Cost modeling", body: "Line-item pricing and workload modeling to compare current invoices against VoiceTel services." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/feature-grid.njk" %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="pricing" aria-labelledby="pricing-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row row--reverse">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
				<h2 id="pricing-heading">Transparent pricing for enterprise planning.</h2>
				<p class="lede">VoiceTel publishes current list rates and provides a pricing calculator for modeling monthly volume by service. The customer portal displays the same rates plus account-specific volume-tier or contract pricing once provisioning is complete. For larger migrations, bring an invoice or recent CDR sample and VoiceTel builds a detailed cost model from actual usage patterns, whether you are comparing current telecom invoices, evaluating multi-location deployments, or preparing a business case for migration.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/pricing/">Pricing calculator</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set rates = [
					{ name: "Outbound minutes", unit: "US local · / min", id: "voice-out-us50", star: true },
					{ name: "Inbound minutes", unit: "US local · / min", id: "voice-in-local", star: true },
					{ name: "Local number", unit: "/ number / month", id: "did-local", star: true },
					{ name: "E911 record", unit: "/ record / month", id: "e911" },
					{ name: "PBX tenant", unit: "/ tenant / month", id: "pbx-tenant" },
					{ name: "Outbound SMS", unit: "/ segment", id: "sms-out", star: true }
				] %}
				{%- set rateFootnote = "List rates. Volume tiers apply automatically in the <a href=\"/pricing/\">pricing calculator</a>; the portal shows your account-specific tier or contract pricing." %}
				{% include "partials/v2/price-table.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="operator" aria-labelledby="operator-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">Operator support</p>
				<h2 id="operator-heading">Work with a telecom operator, not a qualification script.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Enterprise communications require more than a sales workflow: people who understand carrier operations, SIP behavior, routing, porting, emergency-service configuration, and the application layer employees use every day. VoiceTel has operated since 1999, and support is built around engineers who understand SIP traces, carrier responses, and network behavior, for both strategic planning and technical execution.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/enterprise/">All enterprise workstreams</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set kpis = [
					{ label: "Operating since", value: "1999", sub: years ~ " years in continuous operation" },
					{ label: "Colocation POPs", value: (site.pops | length), sub: (site.pops | join(" · ")) },
					{ label: "Cloud regions", value: (site.cloudRegions | length), sub: (site.cloudRegions | join(" · ")) },
					{ label: "Escalations reach", value: "Engineers", sub: "SIP traces · carrier responses · network behavior" }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/kpi-grid.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="cta-band">
			<div class="cta-band__text">
				<h3 class="cta-band__title">Plan the migration.</h3>
				<p class="cta-band__body">Bring an invoice or recent CDR sample; we'll build a detailed cost model from your actual usage.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="cta-band__actions cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Contact us {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/pricing/">Pricing calculator</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
